 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "`:transport-equipment-repair-governor` is implemented end-to-end in
 `src/transport_equipment_repair` as a REPAIR-SHOP OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor -- Repair Advisor (LLM proposal-only) ⊣ Repair
 Governor (closed-op-allowlist / asset-verification / legal-basis /
 unresolved-concern hard-gates). ISIC 3315 covers repair of TRANSPORT
 EQUIPMENT, EXCEPT MOTOR VEHICLES specifically -- ships and boats,
 aircraft and spacecraft, and railway locomotives and rolling stock --
 distinct from sibling repair classes 3311 (fabricated metal products,
 already :implemented), 3312 (machinery and equipment), 3313 (electronic
 and optical equipment), 3314 (electrical equipment) and the residual
 class 3319 (other equipment), and distinct from motor-vehicle repair
 (a different ISIC section entirely). This actor deliberately holds NO
 repair-equipment control authority and NO airworthiness/seaworthiness/
 rail-safety-certification-authority (both are HARD, permanent governor
 blocks, never overridable by human approval -- see `transport-
 equipment-repair.governor` ns docstring), the SAME coordination-only,
 narrower-than-4211 shape `cloud-itonami-isic-3311` (Repair of Fabricated
 Metal Products), `cloud-itonami-isic-3314` (Repair of Electrical
 Equipment) and `cloud-itonami-isic-3319` (Repair of Other Equipment)
 already established in this fleet. Every one of its four proposal ops
 (`:log-repair-record` / `:schedule-repair-operation` / `:flag-safety-
 concern` / `:coordinate-return-to-service`) carries `:effect :propose`
 ONLY -- the governor HARD-holds any proposal that doesn't
 (`effect-not-propose-violations`), a structural invariant distinguishing
 this actor from siblings that DO commit real-world actuation effects.

 UNLIKE `cloud-itonami-isic-3311`'s equivalent check (which exempts
 `:log-repair-record`), this actor's asset-verification HARD check
 applies to ALL FOUR ops -- a repair-order/asset record must be
 independently verified/registered BEFORE ANY action, a genuine,
 documented domain-design requirement broader than 3311's own (see
 `transport-equipment-repair.governor` ns docstring check 4). Like
 `cloud-itonami-isic-3311`/`cloud-itonami-isic-3314`/`cloud-itonami-isic-
 3319`, this actor's `:schedule-repair-operation` AND `:coordinate-
 return-to-service` MAY auto-commit at phase 3 when the governor is
 completely clean -- asset independently verified, a per-(jurisdiction,
 asset-class) pre-return-to-service inspection legal basis on file, and
 no unresolved safety concern on record. Both ops are still only ever a
 proposed diagnostic/repair/testing WINDOW or a proposed completed-unit
 return-to-customer LOGISTICS coordination (pickup/delivery scheduling,
 customer notification) -- NEVER a repair-equipment control command or
 an airworthiness/seaworthiness/rail-safety-certification-authority
 sign-off -- and this actor's own HARD checks (asset-verification,
 legal-basis-on-file, no-unresolved-safety-concern) plus its forbidden-
 action-class block on every certification-authority-decision marker
 already gate the actual structural/airworthiness/seaworthiness/rail-
 safety hazard surface independently of phase. `:flag-safety-concern` is
 the ONLY permanent, unconditional `high-stakes` member in `transport-
 equipment-repair.governor` -- see that ns docstring 'Actuation' section
 for the full rationale.

 Per-(jurisdiction, asset-class) (JPN/USA/DEU x marine-vessel/aircraft/
 railway-rolling-stock -- 9 seeded pairs) post-repair inspection-before-
 return-to-service legal-basis catalog (`transport-equipment-repair.
 facts`) with real official sources, verified via live web search before
 the catalog was written -- all NINE seeded pairs are honestly
 `:qualitative` here (a procedural inspection/certification/release-to-
 service duty, not a fixed numeric notice-lead-time), the same honest-
 coverage convention `installation.facts`/`demolition.facts`/
 `construction.facts`/`fabricated-metal-repair.facts`/`electrical-
 equipment-repair.facts`/`other-equipment-repair.facts` establish. UNLIKE
 `fabricated-metal-repair.facts` (a flat iso3 -> basis map), this
 catalog is keyed `iso3 -> asset-class -> basis-map` because ships,
 aircraft and railway rolling stock genuinely sit under structurally
 disjoint regulatory regimes (classification-society/flag-administration
 survey; airworthiness-authority release-to-service; rail-safety-
 authority maintenance certification) even within the SAME jurisdiction
 -- citing one combined law per jurisdiction would be dishonest. This
 actor does not invent a numeric lead-time count where none of its nine
 researched (jurisdiction, asset-class) sources gives one. This build
 ships NO JVM-only interop anywhere in `src/` (no real Resend/Twilio
 transports -- `transport-equipment-repair.notify` ships only the
 portable mock notifier) per this workspace's cljs-first `.cljc`
 runtime-priority rule. `:flag-safety-concern` ALWAYS escalates to a
 human, at every phase, unconditionally. See `docs/` -- README
 `Actuation` section -- for the full governor-check enumeration and the
 rationale for each hard/soft rule."}
